{"code":"CPSCI 130","title":"Prealgorithms","department":"Computer Science","credits":1,"description":"Foundations of computational problem solving and mathematical techniques commonly used in computer science. Emphasis on analytical and logical skills, including an introduction to Boolean logic and proof techniques. Topics include set theory, permutations and combinations, mathematical induction, asymptotic analysis, recursion, regular expressions, searching and sorting, basic data structures, and graph theory. Topics are reinforced through extensive experiments in Python and Jupyter Notebooks, as well as a brief sojourn into functional programming. Prepares students for 200- and 300-level courses requiring mathematical underpinnings of computer science.Three hours of lecture and two hours of laboratory.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/cpsci-computer-science/100/cpsci-130","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":null,"capacity":40,"comments":null,"end_time":"10:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"type":"LEC","building":null,"end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"10:50","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"10:00"}],"start_time":"10:00:00","instructors":["Shawn Chen"]}]},
{"code":"CPSCI 130L","title":"Prealgorithms Lab","department":"Computer Science","credits":0,"description":null,"cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/cpsci-computer-science/100/cpsci-130","sections":[{"days":"M","room":null,"types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":null,"capacity":20,"comments":null,"end_time":"16:00:00","meetings":[{"days":"M","room":null,"type":"LAB","building":null,"end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"16:00","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"14:00"}],"start_time":"14:00:00","instructors":["Thomas M. Helmuth"]},{"days":"T","room":null,"types":[],"status":"open","section":"02","building":null,"capacity":20,"comments":null,"end_time":"16:00:00","meetings":[{"days":"T","room":null,"type":"LAB","building":null,"end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"16:00","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"14:00"}],"start_time":"14:00:00","instructors":["Thomas M. Helmuth"]}]},
{"code":"CPSCI 200","title":"Ssih Course","department":"Computer Science","credits":0,"description":"This course is taken concurrently with a course approved for the student by the department that aims to satisfy the department's Social, Structural, and Institutional Hierarchies requirement. Satisfactory completion of this course requires successful completion of the approved course. This course should be completed by the end of the student's junior year. Open to concentrators only.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/cpsci-computer-science/200/cpsci-200","sections":[{"days":null,"room":null,"types":["Soc, Struct & Inst Hier"],"status":"open","section":"01","building":null,"capacity":40,"comments":"Open to Computer Science Majors Only","end_time":null,"meetings":[],"start_time":null,"instructors":["Darren J. Strash"]}]},
{"code":"CPSCI 220","title":"Prin Programming Lang","department":"Computer Science","credits":1,"description":"Investigation into the nature, features, design and implementation of programming languages. Students will gain experience with a wide variety of programming languages through programming exercises. Topics will include, among others, object-oriented programming, functional programming, higher-order functions, type systems and polymorphism.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/cpsci-computer-science/200/cpsci-220","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":null,"capacity":20,"comments":"Instructor's signature required during schedule adjustment.","end_time":"13:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"type":"LEC","building":null,"end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"13:50","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"13:00"}],"start_time":"13:00:00","instructors":["Sarah Morrison-Smith"]}]},
{"code":"CPSCI 230","title":"Algorithms & Data Structures","department":"Computer Science","credits":1,"description":"A study of fundamental algorithms and data structures from the canon, emphasizing correctness, and trade-offs between techniques, alongside deliberate coverage of topics from discrete mathematics. Topics include running time and space analysis, invariants as a means of proving correctness, and the divide-and-conquer, greedy, and dynamic programming algorithm design paradigms. Specific problems include graph traversals, (optimal) sorting/searching, minimum spanning tree and shortest paths, longest common subsequences, balanced search trees, heaps, hashing, and union-find for disjoint sets.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/cpsci-computer-science/200/cpsci-230","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"types":["Quantitative & Symbolic R"],"status":"open","section":"01","building":null,"capacity":20,"comments":"Instructor's signature required during schedule adjustment.","end_time":"10:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"type":"LEC","building":null,"end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"10:50","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"10:00"}],"start_time":"10:00:00","instructors":["Christina Ji"]}]},
{"code":"CPSCI 250","title":"Systems","department":"Computer Science","credits":1,"description":"A study of computer systems and the distributed nature of modern computing. Through mastery of the material, students will become more effective programmers by gaining the ability to reason about different layers of software and hardware, enabling them to approach problem-solving through a wider lens. This course includes topics such as performance evaluation and optimization, memory organization and management, parallel and distributed computing, databases, filesystems, computer networks and protocols, and event-driven style programming. For their final projects, students will apply these concepts to build an interactive and distributed application. This course prepares students to take upper level systems electives, such as computer networks, operating systems, and computer architecture.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/cpsci-computer-science/200/cpsci-250","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":null,"capacity":20,"comments":null,"end_time":"11:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"type":"LEC","building":null,"end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"11:50","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"11:00"}],"start_time":"11:00:00","instructors":["Karyn Doke","Han Dong"]}]},
{"code":"CPSCI 270","title":"Artificial Intelligence","department":"Computer Science","credits":1,"description":"A survey of foundational and modern approaches to artificial intelligence. AI methods that tackle a variety of problems with no known efficient algorithms will be discussed, analyzed, and implemented. Students will learn to select an appropriate AI representation to solve a problem and empirically analyze the performance of their implementations. Students will learn to write technical reports explaining their systems and experiments. Topics include heuristic search, game AI, evolutionary computation, machine learning, and the ethics of artificial intelligence. Prepares students to take upper level AI electives.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/cpsci-computer-science/200/cpsci-270","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":null,"capacity":20,"comments":null,"end_time":"09:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"type":"LEC","building":null,"end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"09:50","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"09:00"}],"start_time":"09:00:00","instructors":["Thomas M. Helmuth"]}]},
{"code":"CPSCI 298","title":"Computer Science Research","department":"Computer Science","credits":0.25,"description":"Independent work on a research project under supervision of a faculty member.\n\nStudents may repeat 298 for credit, but only a maximum of one credit of Computer Science Research can count towards satisfying the requirements for departmental honors.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/cpsci-computer-science/200/cpsci-298","sections":[{"days":null,"room":null,"types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":null,"capacity":40,"comments":null,"end_time":null,"meetings":[],"start_time":null,"instructors":["Darren J. Strash"]},{"days":null,"room":null,"types":[],"status":"open","section":"02","building":null,"capacity":40,"comments":null,"end_time":null,"meetings":[],"start_time":null,"instructors":["Christina Ji"]}]},
{"code":"CPSCI 330","title":"Algorithms","department":"Computer Science","credits":1,"description":"A discussion of modern algorithms and advanced techniques, with analysis of time and space complexity in theory and practice. Topics will include, among others: geometric algorithms, graph algorithms, hashing, parallel algorithms, external memory algorithms, parameterized algorithms, and techniques for solving NP-hard problems in practice.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/cpsci-computer-science/300/cpsci-330","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":null,"capacity":20,"comments":"Instructor's signature required during schedule adjustment.","end_time":"11:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"type":"LEC","building":null,"end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"11:50","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"11:00"}],"start_time":"11:00:00","instructors":["Shawn Chen"]}]},
{"code":"CPSCI 390","title":"Computer Networks","department":"Computer Science","credits":1,"description":"This course covers the fundamental concepts of data communication and computer networks. Topics include layered network architecture; reliable data transfer and transport protocols; routing and forwarding; data link layer communications and principles of shared media access. Advanced topics may include physical layer protocols, mobile networks, and software-defined radio networks. Students will apply their understanding of networking fundamentals while working on hands-on programming assignments.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/cpsci-computer-science/300/cpsci-390","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":null,"capacity":20,"comments":"Instructor's signature required during schedule adjustment.","end_time":"09:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"type":"LEC","building":null,"end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"09:50","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"09:00"}],"start_time":"09:00:00","instructors":["Karyn Doke"]}]},
{"code":"CPSCI 410","title":"Senior Seminar","department":"Computer Science","credits":1,"description":"Practicum in which teams of students provide computer expertise and support for faculty research projects. Topics include software engineering analysis, design, coding, testing, maintenance, and documentation. Open to senior concentrators only.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/cpsci-computer-science/400/cpsci-410","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":null,"capacity":12,"comments":"Open to CPSCI Seniors only","end_time":"10:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"type":"LEC","building":null,"end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"10:50","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"10:00"}],"start_time":"10:00:00","instructors":["Han Dong"]},{"days":"MWF","room":null,"types":[],"status":"open","section":"02","building":null,"capacity":12,"comments":"Open to CPSCI Seniors only","end_time":"10:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"type":"LEC","building":null,"end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"10:50","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"10:00"}],"start_time":"10:00:00","instructors":["Wenbo Wang"]}]},
