{"code":"MUSIC 165","title":"Latin American Music","department":"Music","credits":1,"description":"Through the lens of musicology and ethnomusicology, this course explores folk/vernacular, popular, and classical music from various Latin American locales and Latino societies in the U.S. Lessons and readings include genres, instruments, and performance practices as well as contextualization with history, politics, and entertainment. Course also interrogates what defines Latin American and Latino musical identities. The course includes in-class, hands-on performances. No ability to read music is required.","cross_listed":["LTAM 165"],"catalog_url":null,"sections":[{"days":"TR","room":"106","types":["Soc, Struct & Inst Hier"],"status":"waitlisted","section":"01","building":"List Center","capacity":40,"comments":null,"end_time":"10:15:00","meetings":[{"days":"TR","room":"106","type":"LEC","building":"List Center","end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"10:15","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"09:00"}],"start_time":"09:00:00","instructors":["Alex Badue"]}]},
{"code":"MUSIC 181","title":"Basic Keyboard Skills","department":"Music","credits":0.25,"description":"Introduction to keyboard skills including note identification, intervals, major and minor scales, triad identification, 7th chords, simple chord progressions and basic sight-reading. One-quarter course credit. May be repeated for credit with consent of instructor.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/music-theory-and-composition/100/music-181","sections":[{"days":null,"room":null,"types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":null,"capacity":40,"comments":"Instructor's Signature Required. See the MUSIC department for more information.","end_time":null,"meetings":[],"start_time":null,"instructors":["Stephen H. Best"]}]},
{"code":"MUSIC 217","title":"Roots to Country Music","department":"Music","credits":1,"description":"Study of country music from its roots in cowboy songs, fiddle tunes, blues, bluegrass, and gospel hymns to current artists like The [Dixie] Chicks, Taylor Swift, and Brad Paisley. Artists include the Carter Family, Hank Williams, Patsy Cline, Dolly Parton, Willie Nelson, Emmylou Harris, Lynyrd Skynyrd, & Garth Brooks. Study of the musical elements, social class, gender roles, and cultural contexts of styles such as Western Swing, Honky-Tonk, Rockabilly, the Nashville Sound, Southern Rock, and Alt-country. Includes films such as \"Coal Miner's Daughter,\" \"Nashville,\" and \"O Brother, Where Art Thou?\" No previous knowledge of music required. MUSIC-217 has an additional independent project. Registration at the 200-level only with instructor's permission.","cross_listed":["AMST 217"],"catalog_url":null,"sections":[{"days":"TR","room":"106","types":["American Studies"],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"List Center","capacity":40,"comments":"Open to Srs, Jrs, Sophomores, & 1st Yrs. Open to Music majors/minors only or instructor permission.","end_time":"15:45:00","meetings":[{"days":"TR","room":"106","type":"LEC","building":"List Center","end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"15:45","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"14:30"}],"start_time":"14:30:00","instructors":["Lydia R. Hamessley"]}]},
{"code":"MUSIC 221","title":"From Bach to Bartok","department":"Music","credits":1,"description":"Instrumental music from the eighteenth, nineteenth, and first half of the twentieth centuries with an emphasis on orchestral works by composers such as Bach, Mozart, Beethoven, Schubert, Brahms, Mahler, Debussy, Stravinsky, and Bartk. Attention also given to piano and chamber works, including music by women composers. Consideration of the history and development of musical instruments and the use of instrumental classical music in popular culture (as in the films Apocalypse Now, The Shining, 2001: A Space Odyssey, Platoon).","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/music-literature-and-history-of-music/200/music-221","sections":[{"days":"TR","room":"106","types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"List Center","capacity":40,"comments":null,"end_time":"11:45:00","meetings":[{"days":"TR","room":"106","type":"LEC","building":"List Center","end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"11:45","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"10:30"}],"start_time":"10:30:00","instructors":["Alex Badue"]}]},
{"code":"MUSIC 225","title":"Solo Performance","department":"Music","credits":0.25,"description":"The study of music through lessons in voice, flute, oboe, clarinet, bassoon, saxophone, horn, trumpet, trombone, euphonium, tuba, piano, organ, harp, percussion, classical guitar, jazz/contemporary guitar, folk guitar, violin, viola, cello, and contrabass. Half-hour tutorial for one-quarter credit. Students must participate in at least one public performance per semester. A fee is charged. Prerequisites, consent of instructor. Successful completion of Music 110, 210, 211, or the music theory placement exam must occur within three semesters of Solo Performance study. May be repeated for credit. A fee is charged.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/music-performance/200/music-225","sections":[{"days":null,"room":null,"types":["Solo Performance"],"status":"open","section":"90","building":null,"capacity":40,"comments":"Registration will begin in January. Instructor's Signature Required.","end_time":null,"meetings":[],"start_time":null,"instructors":[]}]},
{"code":"MUSIC 226","title":"Solo Performance","department":"Music","credits":0.5,"description":"The study of music through lessons in voice, flute, oboe, clarinet, bassoon, saxophone, horn, trumpet, trombone, euphonium, tuba, piano, organ, harp, percussion, classical guitar, jazz/contemporary guitar, folk guitar, violin, viola, cello, and contrabass. Hour tutorial for one-half credit. Students must participate in at least one public performance per semester. A fee is charged. Prerequisites, consent of instructor. Successful completion of Music 110, 210, 211, or the music theory placement exam must occur within three semesters of Solo Performance study. May be repeated for credit. A fee is charged.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/music-performance/200/music-226","sections":[{"days":null,"room":null,"types":["Solo Performance"],"status":"open","section":"90","building":null,"capacity":40,"comments":"Registration will begin in January. Instructor's Signature Required.","end_time":null,"meetings":[],"start_time":null,"instructors":[]}]},
{"code":"MUSIC 231","title":"Intermed Media: New Frontiers","department":"Music","credits":1,"description":"This class will survey and create emergent and non -linear forms of storytelling using digital and hybrid tools. We will examine notions of narrative authority and hybridity in a digital age and think through different ways we might use technology to distill, break apart or reify modes of communication and visual metaphor. Discussion will push boundaries of traditional storytelling and consider connectivity, liveness and embodied presence. This course will draw on multiple forms of expression including but not limited to digital media, performance, sound, XR, web and network environments.","cross_listed":["DARTS 231","THETR 231"],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/music-performance/200/music-231","sections":[{"days":"R","room":"143","types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Kennedy Center Theatre/Arts","capacity":16,"comments":null,"end_time":"16:00:00","meetings":[{"days":"R","room":"143","type":"STU","building":"Kennedy Center Theatre/Arts","end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"16:00","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"13:00"},{"days":"R","room":"124","type":"STU","building":"Kennedy Center Theatre/Arts","end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"16:00","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"13:00"}],"start_time":"13:00:00","instructors":["Anna Huff"]}]},
{"code":"MUSIC 242","title":"Adv. Group Performance","department":"Music","credits":0.25,"description":"The study of music through chamber performance in one or more of the following: Instrumental Chamber Ensembles (Buchman), Hamilton Voices (Botha), Jazz Combo (Woods). Co-requisite, concurrent registration in the corresponding Group Performance ensemble required; i.e., Orchestra, College Choir or Jazz Ensemble respectively, and consent of instructor. One-quarter course credit each semester. May be repeated. Students may count up to four credits from among 141, 142, 241 and 242 toward graduation.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":null,"sections":[{"days":"MW","room":"HALL","types":["Group Performance"],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Wellin Hall","capacity":40,"comments":null,"end_time":"18:00:00","meetings":[{"days":"MW","room":"HALL","type":"LEC","building":"Wellin Hall","end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"18:00","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"17:00"},{"days":"MW","room":"201","type":"LEC","building":"Schambach Center","end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"18:00","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"17:00"}],"start_time":"17:00:00","instructors":["Charlotte Botha"]},{"days":null,"room":null,"types":["Group Performance"],"status":"open","section":"09A","building":null,"capacity":40,"comments":null,"end_time":null,"meetings":[],"start_time":null,"instructors":["Allan B. Kolsky"]},{"days":null,"room":null,"types":["Group Performance"],"status":"open","section":"09B","building":null,"capacity":40,"comments":null,"end_time":null,"meetings":[],"start_time":null,"instructors":["Cornelia L. Brewster"]},{"days":null,"room":null,"types":["Group Performance"],"status":"open","section":"09C","building":null,"capacity":40,"comments":null,"end_time":null,"meetings":[],"start_time":null,"instructors":["Heather R. Buchman"]},{"days":null,"room":null,"types":["Group Performance"],"status":"open","section":"09D","building":null,"capacity":40,"comments":null,"end