{"code":"NEURO 329","title":"Stress & Psychophysiology","department":"Neuroscience","credits":1,"description":"A theoretical and methodological exploration of the psychological and physiological mechanisms of stress. Questions will include: How does psychological stress impact health and well-being? What neurobiological mechanisms are involved? What is the role of environmental context? Laboratory exercises will include designing original experiments to examine the role of stress on behavior and physiological activity, as well as analyzing data, writing papers based on findings, and oral and poster presentations. Three hours of class and three hours of laboratory. Does not count toward the lab requirement in Psychology.","cross_listed":["PSYCH 329"],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/neuro-neuroscience/300/neuro-329","sections":[{"days":"TR","room":null,"types":["Quantitative & Symbolic R"],"status":"waitlisted","section":"01","building":null,"capacity":20,"comments":null,"end_time":"10:15:00","meetings":[{"days":"TR","room":null,"type":"LEC","building":null,"end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"10:15","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"09:00"},{"days":"M","room":null,"type":"LAB","building":null,"end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"16:00","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"13:00"}],"start_time":"09:00:00","instructors":["Kelly E. Faig"]}]},
{"code":"NEURO 330","title":"Systems Neuroscience","department":"Neuroscience","credits":1,"description":"The primary focus of this course is on the physiological and chemical basis of behavior from a systems perspective. Topics include analysis of sensory and motor systems; motivated behaviors; stress, anxiety and mental illness; and learning and memory. Laboratory exercises introduce students to the anatomy and physiology of the mammalian central nervous system and to some of the principal techniques used in systems and behavioral neuroscience. Three hours of class and three hours of laboratory. Does not count toward the lab requirement in Psychology.","cross_listed":["BIO 330","PSYCH 330"],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/neuro-neuroscience/300/neuro-330","sections":[{"days":"TR","room":null,"types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":null,"capacity":10,"comments":null,"end_time":"11:45:00","meetings":[{"days":"TR","room":null,"type":"LEC","building":null,"end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"11:45","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"10:30"},{"days":"T","room":"3087","type":"LAB","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"16:00","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"13:00"}],"start_time":"10:30:00","instructors":["Abigail K. Myers"]},{"days":"TR","room":null,"types":[],"status":"open","section":"02","building":null,"capacity":10,"comments":null,"end_time":"11:45:00","meetings":[{"days":"TR","room":null,"type":"LEC","building":null,"end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"11:45","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"10:30"},{"days":"W","room":"3087","type":"LAB","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"16:00","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"13:00"}],"start_time":"10:30:00","instructors":["Abigail K. Myers"]}]},
