{"code":"PHYS 136","title":"Physics and Art","department":"Physics","credits":1,"description":"This course is a survey of some of the interesting ways in which fine art intersects math and physics. The curriculum consists of six topics in which some juxtaposition of physics and art is present; in some cases physics is relevant to the context of the art, in some case to the content of the art, and in some cases, both. We begin with some of the earliest works of art and proceed chronologically, including cave paintings and radiocarbon dating, the Archimedes palimpsest and imaging techniques, and the drip paintings of Jackson Pollock and their connection to chaotic motion and fractals. Familiarity with algebra and calculus recommended.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/phys-physics/100/phys-136","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"types":["Quantitative & Symbolic R"],"status":"waitlisted","section":"01","building":null,"capacity":40,"comments":"Open to Srs., Jrs., Soph., & 1st Yr","end_time":"12:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"type":"LEC","building":null,"end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"12:50","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"12:00"}],"start_time":"12:00:00","instructors":["Katherine A. Brown"]}]},
{"code":"PHYS 195","title":"Waves and Fields","department":"Physics","credits":1,"description":"The physics of oscillations, waves and fields. Topics include simple harmonic motion, fluids, sound, electric and magnetic fields, light, optics and interference phenomena. Emphasizes the use of calculus as a tool to describe and analyze the physical world. Three hours of class and three hours of laboratory.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/phys-physics/100/phys-195","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"types":["Qlit Course","Quantitative & Symbolic R"],"status":"open","section":"01","building":null,"capacity":40,"comments":"STUDENTS WHO ENROLL FOR PHYS 195 MUST SIGN UP FOR PHYS 195L","end_time":"10:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":null,"type":"LEC","building":null,"end_date":"2027-05-11","end_time":"10:50","start_date":"2027-01-20","start_time":"10:00"}],"start_time":"10:00:00","instructors":["Seth A. Major"]}]},
